            <ArticleTitle>A trekker in Nepal with painful skin blisters.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2015-210560</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2015210560</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case of a 27-year-old woman trekker with painful, slightly itchy eruptions on the dorsum of both hands for 5 days. On examination, she had a papulovesicular rash with some haemorrhagic vesicles over the dorsum of her hands and thumbs.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
